WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.457
Writing a bid by yourself is a lot of work.

00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:07.950
Velstrian Bid helps a small team do it well, without a bid department.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:14.172
A tender is a formal invitation from a buyer, asking suppliers to bid for a piece of work.

00:00:14.172 --> 00:00:15.900
Start on the Opportunities screen.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:22.122
One search bar covers three official sources: the Find a Tender Service, Contracts Finder, and Public Contracts Scotland.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:27.653
Type what you do, and the closest matches come to the top, ranked against your profile.

00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:29.036
Found a good fit?

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:31.801
Start a bid, and the details carry across.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:33.529
Next, upload the tender pack.

00:00:33.529 --> 00:00:39.751
The pack becomes a clear list of questions, with the work broken into parts, each with an owner.

00:00:39.751 --> 00:00:42.171
Your proof lives in the Evidence Vault.

00:00:42.171 --> 00:00:48.393
Velstrian Bid drafts a first answer grounded in your evidence, and shows which document a point came from.

00:00:48.393 --> 00:00:52.541
You stay in control, you edit, and you keep your own voice.

00:00:52.541 --> 00:00:59.108
For social value, the wider good your work brings, it follows PPN zero two six, the current government guidance.

00:00:59.108 --> 00:01:02.911
Review each answer against its evidence, and bring in a colleague.

00:01:02.911 --> 00:01:06.367
Finally, export a submission ready pack in Word and PDF.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:09.132
Your primary data is stored in the EU.

00:01:09.132 --> 00:01:14.317
Find the right work, answer it with your own evidence, and send a clean submission.

00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:15.700
That is Velstrian Bid.
